# Line endings. The repository and every checkout keep LF: the hooks run under
# bash, which fails on a carriage return (`syntax error near unexpected token
# $'in\r'`), and the mirror, parity and policy-lock gates compare bytes, so a
# `core.autocrlf=true` clone reported hundreds of false drifts.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Client-supplied task material keeps the bytes it was delivered with.
*/Task/** -text

# The memory core is written from PHP Core/ by scripts/core_sync.py (and the
# generator asset by asset_parity.py); the parity gates hold every copy
# byte-identical, so a pull request shows the canonical change once.
# PHP Core/ itself and the two framework-shaped hooks stay reviewed.
